@startuml 06_sequence_signoff
!include ../style.iuml
title Sequence diagram: two-person sign-off of a high-severity finding
autonumber
skinparam maxMessageSize 230

actor "Senior A" as A
actor "Senior B" as B
actor "Senior C" as C
participant "Queue\nservice" as QS
participant "Dispatcher" as DI
database "Store\n(MongoDB)" as DB
participant "Security\nlog" as LOG

== First signature (round 1) ==
DI -> DB : lease of the dossier to senior A
A -> QS : decide_finding for each finding
QS -> DB : decisions of round 1
QS -> DB : leased -> awaiting_countersign\n(first_by = A, answers remembered)
QS -> LOG : claim_signoff (first signature, pending)

== Countersignature (round 2) ==
DI -> DI : exclude A (already decided this dossier)
DI -> DB : lease to senior B
note over B
  B does not see A's answer for the
  high-severity findings.
end note
B -> QS : decide_finding for the high-severity findings
alt B gives the same answer as A for every finding
  QS -> DB : leased -> decided (outcome = agreed)
  QS -> LOG : claim_signoff (countersignature, agreement)
else B contradicts A on at least one finding
  QS -> DB : leased -> ready, escalated = true\n(outcome = disagreed)
  QS -> LOG : claim_signoff (countersignature, disagreement)

  == Tie-break (round 3) ==
  DI -> DI : exclude A and B
  DI -> DB : lease to senior C
  C -> QS : decide_finding for the disputed findings
  QS -> DB : leased -> decided (outcome = tiebreak, final decision)
  QS -> LOG : claim_signoff (tie-break)
end

note over QS
  Safeguards: nobody signs the same dossier twice;
  a level 2 reviewer cannot decide a high-severity
  finding; the level 4 administrator who runs the queue
  decides no dossier.
end note
@enduml
